534
00:40:33.130 --> 00:40:37.292
The second set of risks is about
cost, capacity and features.

535
00:40:37.292 --> 00:40:38.218
Licensing.

536
00:40:38.218 --> 00:40:42.038
Universal DDI uses three
token types, management,

537
00:40:42.038 --> 00:40:45.393
server and reporting,
sold in minimum packs.

538
00:40:45.393 --> 00:40:49.771
Tokens are a subscription entitlement
that expires at the end of the term,

539
00:40:49.771 --> 00:40:53.432
can only be rebalanced within a
type, and overage is handled by

540
00:40:53.432 --> 00:40:57.380
what Infoblox calls True Forward,
on a rolling three-month average.

541
00:40:57.380 --> 00:41:02.157
Model total cost over three to five
years, including the hardware refresh:

542
00:41:02.157 --> 00:41:05.367
Infoblox's end-of-life
policy typically supports

543
00:41:05.367 --> 00:41:08.343
hardware four years after
its last order date.

544
00:41:08.343 --> 00:41:09.768
Reporting capacity.

545
00:41:09.768 --> 00:41:14.393
We covered the ingest caps; five
overruns in thirty days locks reporting.

546
00:41:14.393 --> 00:41:17.481
Size the Reporting tier
for the retention you need,

547
00:41:17.481 --> 00:41:20.129
or make the SIEM the
system of record for logs.

548
00:41:20.129 --> 00:41:25.568
Encrypted DNS needs X6 hardware,
or an extra license on X5.

549
00:41:25.568 --> 00:41:29.780
Plan the refresh around
the encrypted DNS deadline.

550
00:41:29.780 --> 00:41:32.880
DNSSEC defaults to RSA with SHA-1.

551
00:41:32.880 --> 00:41:39.905
Put SHA-256 or ECDSA in the build standard
so nobody signs with the default.

552
00:41:39.905 --> 00:41:44.019
Hybrid limits: the Portal can't
promote a Grid Master Candidate or

553
00:41:44.019 --> 00:41:48.743
manage DHCP failover associations, so
keep Grid Manager runbooks for both.

554
00:41:48.743 --> 00:41:52.311
And stale collateral: an
older Infoblox blog post

555
00:41:52.311 --> 00:41:55.880
still says Universal DDI
isn't FedRAMP compliant.

556
00:41:55.880 --> 00:41:57.905
Cite only the Marketplace record.

557
00:41:57.905 --> 00:42:02.493
On the right are the procurement asks
that turn these risks into obligations.

558
00:42:02.493 --> 00:42:09.005
A FIPS 140-3 certificate timeline, the
versions it covers, and a remedy if it slips.

559
00:42:09.005 --> 00:42:13.230
A BIND advisory SLA with a
KEV not-affected attestation.

560
00:42:13.230 --> 00:42:16.792
The FedRAMP boundary diagram
and a commercial-parity list.

561
00:42:16.792 --> 00:42:19.306
Reporting sized for six months searchable.

562
00:42:19.306 --> 00:42:23.880
Caps on token true-forward, and a clause
guaranteeing you can export your data.

563
